# Privacy & Permission Guardian — managed backend credentials.
#
# Copy this file to `auth.txt` (same directory) and add real users with:
#
#     bun run auth add <username>
#
# One `username:bcrypt-hash` per line. The username is everything before the
# first colon; the hash never contains one. `auth.txt` itself is gitignored —
# a list of hashes in a public repository is an offline cracking exercise.
#
# The line below is an example. Its password is "change-me-please", and it will
# not be accepted: the server rejects any hash it finds in this example file.
demo:$2b$10$vS/A4Jds3d3bO1x/a3/lNe5Z0E7ZN1BORvn5EPBtUQbmzUe2YGGj2
